																			<!-- text start -->
																					<div class="image-editor">
												<p>Today,&nbsp;NBCUniversal&nbsp;announced the launch of&nbsp;<em>Shop What Happens</em>, a first-of-its-kind shoppable Bravo digital series sponsored&nbsp;exclusively&nbsp;by Target&nbsp;the series’ inaugural retail partner.&nbsp;Inspired by&nbsp;Bravo's beloved&nbsp;<em>Watch What Happens Live with Andy Cohen</em>&nbsp;format, the summer-themed weekly series transforms Bravo fandom into real-time shopping action, bringing&nbsp;Bravolebrities,&nbsp;including&nbsp;<strong>Cynthia Bailey</strong>,&nbsp;<strong>Ariana Biermann</strong>,&nbsp;<strong>Lindsay Hubbard</strong>,&nbsp;<strong>Michelle Saniei</strong>, and&nbsp;<strong>Nia Sanchez</strong>,<strong>&nbsp;</strong>together with&nbsp;host&nbsp;<strong>Daryn Carp</strong>&nbsp;for&nbsp;candid conversations, playful games and cultural commentary spanning fashion,&nbsp;entertaining, beauty, travel, swim and seasonal trends&nbsp;–&nbsp;delivering an engaging way for audiences to discover and shop curated Target products featuring stylish, trend-forward finds inspired by the Bravo moments and summer trends they love.&nbsp;</p><p>Built for today’s multi-platform viewing habits, the series lives across Peacock, YouTube,&nbsp;TikTok&nbsp;and&nbsp;clips&nbsp;on Instagram,&nbsp;with an immersive shopping experience that moves&nbsp;viewers&nbsp;seamlessly from inspiration to&nbsp;purchase. On the Peacock mobile&nbsp;app&nbsp;and TikTok, content is&nbsp;optimized&nbsp;in a vertical video format designed for mobile-first discovery and engagement. QR codes enable seamless shopping directly from Peacock&nbsp;on living room devices, while text-to-shop and click-to-shop functionality allow fans to instantly&nbsp;shop&nbsp;the&nbsp;featured Target items they&nbsp;see across the Peacock mobile app,&nbsp;YouTube,&nbsp;TikTok&nbsp;and Instagram.&nbsp;&nbsp;</p><p>&nbsp;</p>
											</div>
																				<!-- Text End -->

										<!-- VIDEO Start-->
										
																				<!-- VIDEO END-->

										<!-- 9:16 Video Start -->
																				<!-- 9:16 Video End -->


										<!-- Image Artifacts start -->
																				<!-- Image Artifacts END -->
										<!-- quote Artifacts start -->
																				<!-- quote Artifacts END -->
										<!-- Gallery Start-->
																													<!-- text start -->
																				<!-- Text End -->

										<!-- VIDEO Start-->
										
																				<!-- VIDEO END-->

										<!-- 9:16 Video Start -->
																				<!-- 9:16 Video End -->


										<!-- Image Artifacts start -->
																				<!-- Image Artifacts END -->
										<!-- quote Artifacts start -->
																					<div class="article-author-info">

												<p class="heading">
													<p>“Hosting&nbsp;<em>Shop What Happens</em>&nbsp;is really about bringing Bravo fans closer to the moments they already love, in a way that feels fun and interactive. I love that it’s all centered around conversation, games and culture happening in the moment, and fans can jump in and be part of it as it unfolds.”&nbsp;</p>
												</p>
												<!-- title -->
												<p class="name">
													&ndash;
													Daryn Carp, Entertainment Correspondent and Host, Shop What Happens
												</p>
												<!-- source -->

												<!-- quote -->
											</div>
											<!-- quote -->
																				<!-- quote Artifacts END -->
										<!-- Gallery Start-->
																													<!-- text start -->
																					<div class="image-editor">
												<p>“The Bravo fans are some of the most passionate people ever and have supported me since I have been part&nbsp;of&nbsp;the Bravo family for the last ten years.&nbsp;They follow my journey all year round even when one of my shows isn’t currently on the air,”&nbsp;said&nbsp;<strong>Lindsay Hubbard, Cast Member,&nbsp;</strong><em><strong>Summer House</strong></em><strong>&nbsp;and&nbsp;</strong><em><strong>In The City</strong></em>&nbsp;“Shop What Happens is a perfect example of extending the Bravo universe and it’s exciting to be part of a project that heightens everyone’s experience”&nbsp;&nbsp;</p>
											</div>
																				<!-- Text End -->

										<!-- VIDEO Start-->
										
																				<!-- VIDEO END-->

										<!-- 9:16 Video Start -->
																				<!-- 9:16 Video End -->


										<!-- Image Artifacts start -->
																				<!-- Image Artifacts END -->
										<!-- quote Artifacts start -->
																				<!-- quote Artifacts END -->
										<!-- Gallery Start-->
																													<!-- text start -->
																				<!-- Text End -->

										<!-- VIDEO Start-->
										
																				<!-- VIDEO END-->

										<!-- 9:16 Video Start -->
																				<!-- 9:16 Video End -->


										<!-- Image Artifacts start -->
																				<!-- Image Artifacts END -->
										<!-- quote Artifacts start -->
																					<div class="article-author-info">

												<p class="heading">
													<p>“At Target, we're continually finding new ways to meet guests where they are, delivering inspiring experiences that make it easy to discover what's trending. Shop What Happens brings together the cultural&nbsp;conversations&nbsp;audiences are already following with the stylish, affordable products they love from Target. By combining trend-forward curation, entertaining content and seamless shopping, we're making it easier than ever for guests to discover products and trends in a way that feels fun, inspiring and uniquely Target."&nbsp;</p>
												</p>
												<!-- title -->
												<p class="name">
													&ndash;
													Michelle Mesenburg, Chief Brand Officer, Target
												</p>
												<!-- source -->

												<!-- quote -->
											</div>
											<!-- quote -->
																				<!-- quote Artifacts END -->
										<!-- Gallery Start-->
																													<!-- text start -->
																					<div class="image-editor">
												<p>“For a century, NBCUniversal&nbsp;has understood that must-see storytelling captures attention and drives action,”&nbsp;said&nbsp;<strong>Karen Kovacs, President, Advertising and Partnerships, NBCUniversal</strong>. “Launching&nbsp;<em>Shop What Happens</em>&nbsp;reflects&nbsp;that belief, expanding what’s possible when premium content, fandom and commerce come together.&nbsp;In partnership with Target,&nbsp;we’re&nbsp;continuing to push the boundaries of shoppable entertainment,&nbsp;meeting audiences where they are and inviting them to engage, explore and&nbsp;shop.”&nbsp;</p><p>Fans can catch new episodes every Sunday for five consecutive weeks beginning June 14&nbsp;streaming&nbsp;on Peacock,&nbsp;YouTube&nbsp;and TikTok.&nbsp;&nbsp;</p><p>The launch of “Shop What Happens” builds on NBCUniversal’s longstanding leadership in commerce innovation.&nbsp;As the first media company to bring&nbsp;ShoppableTV&nbsp;to market, NBCUniversal continues to deliver&nbsp;cutting-edge&nbsp;solutions that inspire viewers and enable seamless conversion for brands.&nbsp;To date, NBCUniversal’s commerce business has driven strong demand and measurable impact across brands of all sizes, collapsing the purchase funnel with a&nbsp;<strong>+378%</strong>&nbsp;increase in engagement when storytelling, IP and talent are&nbsp;leveraged, and&nbsp;<strong>+60%&nbsp;</strong>year-over-year purchase&nbsp;growth.&nbsp;</p>
											</div>
																				<!-- Text End -->

										<!-- VIDEO Start-->
										
																				<!-- VIDEO END-->

										<!-- 9:16 Video Start -->
																				<!-- 9:16 Video End -->


										<!-- Image Artifacts start -->
																				<!-- Image Artifacts END -->
										<!-- quote Artifacts start -->
																				<!-- quote Artifacts END -->
										<!-- Gallery Start-->
																													<!-- text start -->
																					<div class="image-editor">
												<p><strong>Launching this season:&nbsp;</strong>&nbsp;</p><ul type="disc"><li><strong>#101 Summer Fashion: Sunday, June 14</strong>&nbsp;</li></ul><p><em>Summer House</em>&nbsp;and&nbsp;<em>In&nbsp;The&nbsp;City’</em>s Lindsay Hubbard weighs in on this summer's&nbsp;must-have fashion finds, favorite&nbsp;picks&nbsp;and personal style insights.&nbsp;</p><ul type="disc"><li><strong>#102 Summer Hosting: Sunday, June 21</strong>&nbsp;</li></ul><p><em>The Real Housewives of Atlanta</em>’s Cynthia Bailey explores the essentials for the perfect summer&nbsp;party&nbsp;from effortless summer entertaining must-haves to seasonal favorites.&nbsp;</p><ul type="disc"><li><strong>#103 Travel &amp; Swim: Sunday, June 28</strong>&nbsp;</li></ul><p><em>The Valley</em>’s Michelle Saniei unpacks&nbsp;beach accessories and vacation-ready&nbsp;favorites, from poolside&nbsp;staples&nbsp;to travel-friendly finds perfect&nbsp;for summer&nbsp;adventures. &nbsp;</p><ul type="disc"><li><strong>#104 Beauty: Sunday, July 5</strong>&nbsp;</li></ul><p><em>Next Gen NYC</em>’s Ariana Biermann spills her take on the beauty trends, glam&nbsp;essentials&nbsp;and self-care must-haves&nbsp;everyone is talking about for the best sun-kissed glow.&nbsp;&nbsp;</p><ul type="disc"><li><strong>#105 Summer Trends: Sunday, July 12</strong>&nbsp;</li></ul><p><em>The Valley</em>’s Nia Sanchez breaks down&nbsp;the trends, styles,&nbsp;and&nbsp;finds heating up summer that&nbsp;are&nbsp;worth adding to cart.&nbsp;&nbsp;</p>
											</div>
																				<!-- Text End -->

										<!-- VIDEO Start-->
										
																				<!-- VIDEO END-->

										<!-- 9:16 Video Start -->
																				<!-- 9:16 Video End -->


